course: dictionary
lesson: 8133
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word replay can mean different things, and the sentence tells you which one. The prefix re- means again, so a replay is something done again. «Replay it in my head» does not mean playing a game. It means thinking about something again.
explain: «Being laughed at can happen in a second, and then live for days in your head, getting bigger every time you replay it.» Replay here means to think about the moment again and again. Check it: "getting bigger every time you think about it again" makes sense, so that is the meaning.
explain: In sport, a replay is a clip shown again, such as a slow-motion goal. A replay can also be a match played again because the first one was a draw or was stopped. Look at the clues around the word to find out which meaning fits.
fact: Replay means to play something again, such as a video, song or game.
fact: A replay is a recording shown again, especially a moment in sport.
fact: A replay can also be a match that is played again after a draw or a stopped game.
fact: To replay a memory means to keep thinking about it. «The mind often replays embarrassing moments at night.»
fact: The prefix re- means again, so replay, rewrite and redo all mean do again.
exercise: «The referee showed a slow-motion replay of the goal.» What is a replay here? | A new team kit | A player who was sent off | *A clip of the goal shown again | A stadium with lights
exercise: «The cup tie was a draw, so the two teams will play a replay next week.» What does replay mean here? | A video with no sound | *A match played again | A song played on the radio | A goal scored twice
exercise: «He kept replaying the moment in his head all afternoon.» What does replaying mean here? | Forgetting it quickly | Shouting it out loud | Playing a video game | *Thinking about it again and again
test: What does the prefix re- in replay mean? | Not | Very big | *Again | Before
test: «Being laughed at can happen in a second, then live for days in your head.» Here "replay it" means | Laugh out loud | *Think about it again and again | Turn off the phone | Forget it straight away
exam: Which meaning of replay fits «The mind often replays embarrassing moments at night»? | A match that is played again | To record a video for a friend | *To keep thinking about a memory | To sing a song twice
